# Admin app — local overrides (port 4000).
# Supabase credentials and NEXT_PUBLIC_WWW_URL load from the repo root `.env.local` via next.config.ts.
PORT=4000
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_URL=http://localhost:4000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WWW_URL is no longer read by admin. There is no forgot-password or
# sign-up link into the customer app — that cross-link is how staff ended up in
# the buyer flows — and deleting it is independent of ADMIN_LOGIN below.

# Email + password sign-in. Google is the sign-in path (decided 2026-09-04);
# unset or anything other than exactly `true` leaves the login page Google-only.
# Set `true` only where a Google round trip is not available — a local machine
# without a company Google session, or getting in while OAuth is broken.
#
# Server-side (deliberately not NEXT_PUBLIC_): the login page reads it and passes
# a boolean to the form, and `signInInternal` checks it again before touching
# Supabase, so the flag closes the server action and not just the UI. Flipping it
# needs a redeploy.
#
# ⚠️ The password path still requires an `internal_user` row — www customers live
# in the SAME Supabase auth project, so without that check any buyer's password
# would open admin. It does NOT check the email domain; the row is the gate.
# ADMIN_LOGIN=true

# Attachment downloads (PROD-2434). Both load from the repo root `.env.local`,
# shared with www — the admin BFF signs the same HMAC to reach the same backend.
# Without them the file list still renders; only the download button fails, and
# it logs the misconfiguration rather than blaming the rep.
#   BACKEND_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
#   SERVICE_SHARED_SECRET=<same value the backend holds>

# Data source. `mock` (default) reads the allowlist + fixtures below.
# `supabase` reads public.internal_user and public.rfq under RLS (PROD-2415) —
# the switch is this one variable; no component or adapter code changes.
#
# ⚠️ With `supabase`, a sales member sees only requests whose lead is assigned to
# their crm_owner_id. Nothing populates rfq.assigned_owner_crm_id yet (the
# ADR-0012 D3 assignment webhook is unbuilt), so the list is EMPTY until it does.
# That is the scoping working, not a misconfiguration.
ADMIN_DATA_SOURCE=mock

# Mock internal accounts (ADMIN_DATA_SOURCE=mock only).
# Use a real Supabase auth email you can sign in with.
# Format: email:zohoUserId pairs, comma-separated.
# Mock request fixtures for zoho-user-sales-1 live in packages/domain.
ADMIN_INTERNAL_ACCOUNT_ALLOWLIST=your-real-supabase-email@example.com:zoho-user-sales-1

# Development only — never set in production or on Vercel preview deploys you share.
# Skips Supabase login; opens protected pages directly with mock internal session.
ADMIN_DEV_BYPASS=true
ADMIN_DEV_BYPASS_ZOHO_USER_ID=zoho-user-sales-1
